#: src/getting-started.md:408
msgid ""
"In a simplified way, Kubernetes works by allowing you to declare the desired "
"state of your system, and then its controllers continuously observe the "
"cluster and take actions to ensure that the actual state matches the desired "
"state. For your custom APIs and controllers, the process is similar. "
"Remember, you are extending Kubernetes' behaviors and its APIs to fit your "
"specific needs."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started.md:410
msgid "In our controller, we implement a reconciliation process."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started.md:412
msgid ""
"Essentially, the reconciliation process functions as a loop, continuously "
"checking conditions and performing necessary actions until the desired state "
"is achieved. This process will keep running until all conditions in the "
"system align with the desired state defined in our implementation."
msgstr ""

