#: src/cronjob-tutorial/cronjob-tutorial.md:3
msgid ""
"Too many tutorials start out with some really contrived setup, or some toy "
"application that gets the basics across, and then stalls out on the more "
"complicated stuff.  Instead, this tutorial should take you through (almost) "
"the full gamut of complexity with Kubebuilder, starting off simple and "
"building up to something pretty full-featured."
msgstr ""

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/cronjob-tutorial.md:9
msgid ""
"Pretend (and sure, this is a teensy bit contrived) that you have finally "
"gotten tired of the maintenance burden of the non-Kubebuilder implementation "
"of the CronJob controller in Kubernetes, and you'd like to rewrite it using "
"Kubebuilder."
msgstr ""

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/cronjob-tutorial.md:14
msgid ""
"The job (no pun intended) of the _CronJob_ controller is to run one-off "
"tasks on the Kubernetes cluster at regular intervals.  It does this by "
"building on top of the _Job_ controller, whose task is to run one-off tasks "
"once, seeing them to completion."
msgstr ""

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/cronjob-tutorial.md:19
msgid ""
"Instead of trying to tackle rewriting the Job controller as well, use this "
"as an opportunity to see how to interact with external types."
msgstr ""

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/cronjob-tutorial.md:26
msgid ""
"Note that most of this tutorial is generated from literate Go files that "
"live in the book source directory: "
"[docs/book/src/cronjob-tutorial/testdata](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/tree/master/docs/book/src/cronjob-tutorial/testdata). "
" The full, runnable project lives in "
"[project](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/tree/master/docs/book/src/cronjob-tutorial/testdata/project), "
"while intermediate files live directly under the "
"[testdata](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/tree/master/docs/book/src/cronjob-tutorial/testdata) "
"directory."
msgstr ""

