#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:174
msgid "Automation"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:176
msgid ""
"This integrates cleanly with automation. The "
"[`autoupdate.kubebuilder.io/v1-alpha`](./../../plugins/available/autoupdate-v1-alpha.md) "
"plugin can scaffold a GitHub Actions workflow that runs the command on a "
"schedule (e.g., weekly). When a new Kubebuilder release is available, it "
"opens an Issue with a compare link so you can create the PR and review it."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:178
msgid ""
"Changing extra Git configs only during the run (does not change your "
"~/.gitconfig)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:180
msgid ""
"By default, `kubebuilder alpha update` applies safe Git configs: "
"`merge.renameLimit=999999`, `diff.renameLimit=999999`, "
"`merge.conflictStyle=merge` You can add more, or disable them."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:184
msgid "**Add more on top of defaults**"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:190
msgid "**Disable defaults entirely**"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:195
msgid "**Disable defaults and set your own**"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:206
msgid ""
"This command uses `kubebuilder alpha generate` under the hood. We support "
"projects created with <strong>v4.5.0+</strong>. If yours is older, first run "
"`kubebuilder alpha generate` once to modernize the scaffold. After that, you "
"can use `kubebuilder alpha update` for future upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:211
msgid ""
"Projects created with **Kubebuilder v4.6.0+** include `cliVersion` in the "
"`PROJECT` file. The command uses that value to pick the correct CLI for "
"re-scaffolding."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:220
msgid "`--conflict-message`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:220
msgid ""
"Custom commit message for merges with conflicts. Defaults to `:warning: "
"chore(kubebuilder): update scaffold (manual conflict resolution) <from> -> "
"<to>`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:221
msgid "`--force`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:221
msgid ""
"Continue even if merge conflicts happen. Conflicted files are committed with "
"conflict markers (CI/cron friendly)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:222
msgid "`--from-branch`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:222
msgid "Git branch that holds your current project code. Defaults to `main`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:223
msgid "`--from-version`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:223
msgid ""
"Kubebuilder release to update **from** (e.g., `v4.6.0`). If unset, read from "
"the `PROJECT` file when possible."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:224
msgid "`--git-config`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:224
msgid ""
"Repeatable. Pass per-invocation Git config as `-c key=value`. **Default** "
"(if omitted): `-c merge.renameLimit=999999 -c diff.renameLimit=999999`. Your "
"configs are applied on top. To disable defaults, include `--git-config "
"disable`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:225
msgid "`--merge-message`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:225
msgid ""
"Custom commit message for successful merges (no conflicts). Defaults to "
"`chore(kubebuilder): update scaffold <from> -> <to>`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:226
msgid "`--open-gh-issue`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:226
msgid ""
"Create a GitHub issue with a pre-filled checklist and compare link after the "
"update completes (requires `gh`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:227
msgid "`--output-branch`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:227
msgid ""
"Name of the output branch. Default: "
"`kubebuilder-update-from-<from-version>-to-<to-version>`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:228
msgid "`--push`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:228
msgid "Push the output branch to the `origin` remote after the update completes."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:229
msgid "`--restore-path`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:229
msgid ""
"Repeatable. Paths to preserve from the base branch when squashing (e.g., "
"`.github/workflows`). **Not supported** with `--show-commits`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:230
msgid "`--show-commits`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:230
msgid ""
"Keep full history (do not squash). **Not compatible** with `--restore-path`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:231
msgid "`--to-version`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/commands/alpha_update.md:231
msgid ""
"Kubebuilder release to update **to** (e.g., `v4.7.0`). If unset, defaults to "
"the latest available release."
msgstr ""

