#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:3
msgid ""
"Kubebuilder uses a tool called "
"[`controller-gen`](https://sigs.k8s.io/controller-tools \"Controller "
"Tools\") to generate utility code and Kubernetes object YAML, like "
"CustomResourceDefinitions."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:7
msgid ""
"To do this, it makes use of special \"marker comments\" (comments that start "
"with `// +`) to indicate additional information about fields, types, and "
"packages.  In the case of CRDs, these are generally pulled from your "
"`_types.go` files.  For more information on markers, see the [marker "
"reference docs](./markers.md \"Markers for Config/Code Generation\")."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:13
msgid ""
"Kubebuilder provides a `make` target to run controller-gen and generate "
"CRDs: `make manifests`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:16
msgid ""
"When you run `make manifests`, you should see CRDs generated under the "
"`config/crd/bases` directory.  `make manifests` can generate a number of "
"other artifacts as well -- see the [marker reference docs](./markers.md "
"\"Markers for Config/Code Generation\") for more details."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:21
msgid "Validation"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:23
msgid ""
"CRDs support [declarative "
"validation](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/access-kubernetes-api/custom-resources/custom-resource-definitions/#validation "
"\"Custom Resource Definitions: Validation\") using an [OpenAPI v3 "
"schema](https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/master/versions/3.0.0.md#schemaObject "
"\"OpenAPI v3\") in the `validation` section."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:26
msgid ""
"In general, [validation markers](./markers/crd-validation.md) may be "
"attached to fields or to types. If you are defining complex validation, if "
"you need to re-use validation, or if you need to validate slice elements, it "
"is often best to define a new type to describe your validation."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:31 src/reference/generating-crd.md:107
#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:128 src/reference/metrics.md:437
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:35
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:validation:MaxLength=15\n"
"\t// +kubebuilder:validation:MinLength=1\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:37
msgid "`json:\"name,omitempty\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:39
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:validation:MaxItems=500\n"
"\t// +kubebuilder:validation:MinItems=1\n"
"\t// +kubebuilder:validation:UniqueItems=true\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:42
msgid "`json:\"knights,omitempty\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:44
msgid "`json:\"alias,omitempty\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:45
msgid "`json:\"rank\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:47
msgid "// +kubebuilder:validation:Enum=Lion;Wolf;Dragon\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:50
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Minimum=1\n"
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Maximum=3\n"
"// +kubebuilder:validation:ExclusiveMaximum=false\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:58
msgid "Additional printer columns"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:60
msgid ""
"Starting with Kubernetes 1.11, `kubectl get` can ask the server what columns "
"to display.  For CRDs, this can be used to provide useful, type-specific "
"information with `kubectl get`, similar to the information provided for "
"built-in types."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:65
msgid ""
"The information that gets displayed can be controlled with the "
"[additionalPrinterColumns "
"field](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/access-kubernetes-api/custom-resources/custom-resource-definitions/#additional-printer-columns "
"\"Custom Resource Definitions: Additional Printer Columns\") on your CRD, "
"which is controlled by the [`+kubebuilder:printcolumn`](./markers/crd.md "
"\"CRD Generation\") marker on the Go type for your CRD."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:71
msgid ""
"For instance, in the following example, add fields to display information "
"about the knights, rank, and alias fields from the validation example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:76
msgid ""
"// "
"+kubebuilder:printcolumn:name=\"Alias\",type=string,JSONPath=`.spec.alias`\n"
"// "
"+kubebuilder:printcolumn:name=\"Rank\",type=integer,JSONPath=`.spec.rank`\n"
"// +kubebuilder:printcolumn:name=\"Bravely Run "
"Away\",type=boolean,JSONPath=`.spec.knights[?(@ == \"Sir "
"Robin\")]`,description=\"when danger rears its ugly head, he bravely turned "
"his tail and fled\",priority=10\n"
"// "
"+kubebuilder:printcolumn:name=\"Age\",type=\"date\",JSONPath=\".metadata.creationTimestamp\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:90
msgid "Subresources"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:92
msgid ""
"CRDs can choose to implement the `/status` and `/scale` "
"[subresources](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/access-kubernetes-api/custom-resources/custom-resource-definitions/#status-subresource "
"\"Custom Resource Definitions: Status Subresource\") as of Kubernetes 1.13."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:95
msgid ""
"It's generally recommended that you make use of the `/status` subresource on "
"all resources that have a status field."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:98
msgid ""
"Both subresources have a corresponding [marker](./markers/crd.md \"CRD "
"Generation\")."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:100
msgid "Status"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:102
msgid ""
"You enable the status subresource via `+kubebuilder:subresource:status`. "
"When you enable it, updates at the main resource will not change status. "
"Similarly, updates to the status subresource cannot change anything but the "
"status field."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:110
msgid "// +kubebuilder:subresource:status\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:120
msgid "Scale"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:122
msgid ""
"You enable the scale subresource via `+kubebuilder:subresource:scale`. When "
"you enable it, users can use `kubectl scale` with your resource. If the "
"`selectorpath` argument points to the string form of a label selector, the "
"HorizontalPodAutoscaler can autoscale your resource."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:137
msgid "`json:\"selector\"` // this must be the string form of the selector\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:140
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:subresource:status\n"
"// "
"+kubebuilder:subresource:scale:specpath=.spec.replicas,statuspath=.status.replicas,selectorpath=.status.selector\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:152
msgid "Multiple versions"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:154
msgid ""
"As of Kubernetes 1.13, you can have multiple versions of your Kind defined "
"in your CRD, and use a webhook to convert between them."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:157
msgid ""
"For more details on this process, see the [multiversion "
"tutorial](/multiversion-tutorial/tutorial.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:160
msgid ""
"By default, Kubebuilder disables generating different validation for "
"different versions of the Kind in your CRD, to be compatible with older "
"Kubernetes versions."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:164
msgid ""
"You'll need to enable this by switching the line in your makefile that says "
"`CRD_OPTIONS ?= \"crd:trivialVersions=true,preserveUnknownFields=false` to "
"`CRD_OPTIONS ?= crd:preserveUnknownFields=false` if using v1beta CRDs, and "
"`CRD_OPTIONS ?= crd` if using v1 (recommended)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:169
msgid ""
"Then, you can use the `+kubebuilder:storageversion` "
"[marker](./markers/crd.md \"CRD Generation\") to indicate the "
"[GVK](/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md \"Group-Version-Kind\") that should be used "
"to store data by the API server."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:173
msgid "Under the hood"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:175
msgid ""
"Kubebuilder scaffolds out make rules to run `controller-gen`.  The rules "
"will automatically install controller-gen if it is not on your path using "
"`go install` with Go modules."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:179
msgid ""
"You can also run `controller-gen` directly, if you want to see what it is "
"doing."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:182
msgid ""
"Each controller-gen \"generator\" is controlled by an option to "
"controller-gen, using the same syntax as markers. controller-gen also "
"supports different output \"rules\" to control how and where output goes. "
"Notice the `manifests` make rule (condensed slightly to only generate CRDs):"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:188
msgid "# Generate manifests for CRDs"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:190
msgid ""
"manager-role crd webhook paths=\"./...\" "
"output:crd:artifacts:config=config/crd/bases"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/generating-crd.md:193
msgid ""
"It uses the `output:crd:artifacts` output rule to indicate that CRD-related "
"config (non-code) artifacts should end up in `config/crd/bases` instead of "
"`config/crd`."
msgstr ""

