msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:24
msgid ""
"The status subresource allows you to update the status field separately from "
"the rest of the resource spec, and prevents updates to the status "
"subresource when updating the root object. This is useful for separating "
"user-provided spec from system-provided status."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:30
msgid ""
"    // +kubebuilder:subresource:status\n"
"    type MyCRD struct {\n"
"        metav1.TypeMeta\n"
"        metav1.ObjectMeta\n"
"        Spec   MyCRDSpec\n"
"        Status MyCRDStatus\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:40
msgid ""
"The scale subresource allows you to use `kubectl scale` and the "
"HorizontalPodAutoscaler with your CRD."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:44
msgid ""
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:subresource:scale:specpath=.spec.replicas,statuspath=.status.replicas,selectorpath=.status.selector\n"
"    type MyCRD struct {\n"
"        metav1.TypeMeta\n"
"        metav1.ObjectMeta\n"
"        Spec MyCRDSpec\n"
"        Status MyCRDStatus\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:54
msgid ""
"The selector field must be the _string_ form (serialized form) of a "
"selector. Setting a pod label selector is necessary for your type to work "
"with the HorizontalPodAutoscaler. This is typically .status.selector."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:60
msgid ""
"This is where the desired number of replicas is stored (typically "
".spec.replicas)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:64
msgid ""
"This is where the actual number of replicas is stored (typically "
".status.replicas)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:68
msgid ""
"When conversion is enabled for a CRD (i.e. it's not a "
"trivial-versions/single-version CRD), one version is set as the \"storage "
"version\" to be stored in etcd.  Attempting to store any other version will "
"result in conversion to the storage version via a conversion webhook."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:74
msgid ""
"    // +kubebuilder:storageversion\n"
"    type MyCRDv2 struct {\n"
"        metav1.TypeMeta\n"
"        metav1.ObjectMeta\n"
"        Spec MyCRDSpec\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:83
msgid ""
"This is useful if you need to skip generating and listing version entries "
"for 'internal' resource versions, which typically exist if using the "
"Kubernetes upstream conversion-gen tool."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:89
msgid ""
"    // +kubebuilder:skipversion\n"
"    type MyCRDInternal struct {\n"
"        // internal version not served by API\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:96
msgid ""
"Field selectors allow users to filter resources based on field values when "
"listing. For example, `kubectl get mycrds --field-selector "
"status.phase=Running`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:101
msgid ""
"    // +kubebuilder:selectablefield:JSONPath=&#34;.status.phase&#34;\n"
"    type MyCRD struct {\n"
"        metav1.TypeMeta\n"
"        metav1.ObjectMeta\n"
"        Status MyCRDStatus\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:110
msgid "The path is relative to the resource root. Example: `.status.phase`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:116
msgid ""
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:resource:path=mycrdplural,singular=mycrdsingular,shortName=mc;mcrd,categories=all,scope=Namespaced\n"
"    type MyCRD struct {\n"
"        metav1.TypeMeta\n"
"        metav1.ObjectMeta\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:124
msgid ""
"Group aliases are used to work with groups of resources at once. The most "
"common one is \"all\" which covers about a third of the base resources in "
"Kubernetes, and is generally used for \"user-facing\" resources. This allows "
"users to run commands like `kubectl get all` to include your CRD."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:131
msgid ""
"It generally corresponds to a plural, lower-cased version of the Kind. For "
"example, if the Kind is \"MyCRD\", the path might be \"mycrds\". See "
"https://book.kubebuilder.io/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.html."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:137
msgid ""
"Scope defaults to \"Namespaced\".  Cluster-scoped (\"Cluster\") resources "
"don't exist in namespaces and are accessible from anywhere in the cluster."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:142
msgid ""
"Short names are often used when people have work with your resource over and "
"over again.  For instance, \"rs\" for \"replicaset\" or \"crd\" for "
"customresourcedefinition. Multiple short names can be specified separated by "
"semicolons."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:149
msgid ""
"The singular form is otherwise defaulted off the plural (path). This is used "
"in API responses and `kubectl` output."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:154
msgid ""
"This allows you to customize which columns are shown when users run `kubectl "
"get` on your CRD."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:158
msgid ""
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:printcolumn:name=&#34;Status&#34;,type=string,JSONPath=`.status.phase`\n"
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:printcolumn:name=&#34;Age&#34;,type=date,JSONPath=`.metadata.creationTimestamp`\n"
"    type MyCRD struct {\n"
"        metav1.TypeMeta\n"
"        metav1.ObjectMeta\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:167
msgid ""
"The path is relative to the resource root. Example: `.status.phase` or "
"`.spec.replicas`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:171
msgid ""
"Display behavior is client-dependent; see CustomResourceColumnDefinition in "
"the Kubernetes API docs."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:175
msgid ""
"It may be any OpenAPI data format corresponding to the type, listed at "
"https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/master/versions/2.0.md#data-types."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:180
msgid ""
"Lower priority (_higher_ numbered) columns will be hidden if the terminal "
"width is too small. Priority 0 columns are always shown."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:185
msgid ""
"It may be any OpenAPI data type listed at "
"https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification/blob/master/versions/2.0.md#data-types. "
"Common values: \"string\", \"integer\", \"number\", \"boolean\", \"date\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:191
msgid ""
"For example adding annotation \"api-approved.kubernetes.io\" for a CRD with "
"Kubernetes groups, or annotation \"cert-manager.io/inject-ca-from-secret\" "
"for a CRD that needs CA injection."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:196
msgid ""
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:metadata:annotations=&#34;api-approved.kubernetes.io/v1=https://github.com/myorg/myrepo/pull/123&#34;\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:metadata:labels=&#34;app=myapp&#34;\n"
"    type MyCRD struct {\n"
"        metav1.TypeMeta\n"
"        metav1.ObjectMeta\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:205
msgid ""
"Format: \"key=value\". Multiple annotations can be specified by repeating "
"the marker."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:209
msgid ""
"Format: \"key=value\". Multiple labels can be specified by repeating the "
"marker."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:213 src/reference/markers/crd.md:218
msgid ""
"The url is required and must be a valid URL. The description is optional and "
"provides a short description of the external documentation."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:223
msgid ""
"Deprecated versions show a warning message when used. This is useful for "
"communicating to users that they should migrate to a newer version."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:228
msgid ""
"    // +kubebuilder:deprecatedversion:warning=&#34;v1alpha1 is deprecated; "
"use v1 instead&#34;\n"
"    type MyCRDv1alpha1 struct {\n"
"        metav1.TypeMeta\n"
"        metav1.ObjectMeta\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:236
msgid ""
"This message is displayed to users when they interact with the deprecated "
"version."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:3
msgid ""
"These markers modify how the CRD validation schema is produced for the types "
"and fields they modify.  Each corresponds roughly to an OpenAPI/JSON schema "
"option."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:7
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:6
msgid "See [Generating CRDs](/reference/generating-crd.md) for examples."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:12
msgid ""
"Certain markers may seem duplicated. However, these markers are grouped "
"based on their context of use — such as fields, types, or arrays. For "
"instance, a marker like `+kubebuilder:validation:Enum` can be applied to "
"individual fields or array items, and this flexibility is reflected in the "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:16
msgid ""
"The grouping ensures clarity by showing how the same marker can be reused "
"for different purposes."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:23
msgid ""
"Custom resources are validated using the generated OpenAPI v3 schema and "
"must comply with Kubernetes structural schema rules. Only field types and "
"constraints that can be represented in the CRD schema are enforced by the "
"API server."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:26
msgid ""
"Numeric types are constrained by [Kubernetes CRD OpenAPI v3 schema "
"compatibility](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/extend-kubernetes/custom-resources/custom-resource-definitions/#validation). "
"In practice, prefer Go types that map cleanly to the supported OpenAPI "
"formats (for example, `int32` and `int64` for integers). For values that "
"require decimal-like representation, use `resource.Quantity`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:30
msgid ""
"Use Kubebuilder validation markers to declare additional constraints — such "
"as minimum and maximum values, length limits, patterns, enums, and list or "
"map rules — so they are reflected in the generated CRD and validated at "
"runtime."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:35
msgid ""
"This is often not necessary, but may be helpful with custom serialization."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:39
msgid ""
"    // +nullable\n"
"    Description *string\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:44
#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:105
#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:464
#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:525
