#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:3
msgid ""
"These markers help control how the Kubernetes API server processes API "
"requests involving your custom resources."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:10
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:42
msgid ""
"i.e. whether each field in the struct is independent of the others, or all "
"fields are treated as a single unit."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:13
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:45
msgid ""
"This is important for Server-Side Apply to correctly merge struct updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:15
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:47
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:79
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:105
msgid "Possible values:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:17
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:49
msgid ""
"\"granular\": fields in the struct are independent of each other, and can be "
"manipulated by different actors. This is the default behavior."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:21
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:53
msgid ""
"\"atomic\": all fields are treated as one unit. Any changes have to replace "
"the entire struct."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:26
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:58
msgid ""
"    // Granular struct (default) - individual fields can be updated "
"independently\n"
"    // +structType=granular\n"
"    type Config struct {\n"
"        Host string\n"
"        Port int\n"
"    }\n"
"    \n"
"    // Atomic struct - entire struct is replaced on update\n"
"    // +structType=atomic\n"
"    type Credentials struct {\n"
"        Username string\n"
"        Password string\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:74
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:100
msgid ""
"i.e. whether each item in the map is independent of the others, or all "
"fields are treated as a single unit."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:77
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:103
msgid "This is important for Server-Side Apply to correctly merge map updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:81
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:107
msgid ""
"\"granular\": items in the map are independent of each other, and can be "
"manipulated by different actors. This is the default behavior."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:85
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:111
msgid ""
"\"atomic\": all fields are treated as one unit. Any changes have to replace "
"the entire map."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:90
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:116
msgid ""
"    // Granular map (default) - individual keys can be updated "
"independently\n"
"    // +mapType=granular\n"
"    Labels map[string]string\n"
"    \n"
"    // Atomic map - entire map is replaced on update\n"
"    // +mapType=atomic\n"
"    Config map[string]string\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:126
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:159
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:338
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:371
msgid "represents (map, set, atomic)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:128
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:161
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:340
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:373
msgid "This is important for Server-Side Apply to correctly merge list updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:130
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:163
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:342
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:375
msgid "Possible data-structure types of a list are:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:132
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:165
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:344
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:377
msgid ""
"\"map\": it needs to have a key field, which will be used to build an "
"associative list. A typical example is a the pod container list, which is "
"indexed by the container name."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:136
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:169
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:348
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:381
msgid ""
"\"set\": Fields need to be \"scalar\", and there can be only one occurrence "
"of each."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:139
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:172
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:351
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:384
msgid ""
"\"atomic\": All the fields in the list are treated as a single value, are "
"typically manipulated together by the same actor."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:144
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:177
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:356
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:389
msgid ""
"    // Map list (associative list) - items are merged by key\n"
"    // +listType=map\n"
"    // +listMapKey=name\n"
"    Containers []Container\n"
"    \n"
"    // Set list - items must be unique scalars\n"
"    // +listType=set\n"
"    Tags []string\n"
"    \n"
"    // Atomic list - entire list is replaced on update\n"
"    // +listType=atomic\n"
"    Args []string\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:192
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:211
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:404
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:423
msgid ""
"It indicates the index of a map list. They can be repeated if multiple keys "
"must be used. It can only be used when ListType is set to map, and the keys "
"should be scalar types."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:198
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:217
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:410
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:429
msgid ""
"    // Single key\n"
"    // +listType=map\n"
"    // +listMapKey=name\n"
"    Containers []Container\n"
"    \n"
"    // Composite key (multiple keys)\n"
"    // +listType=map\n"
"    // +listMapKey=name\n"
"    // +listMapKey=protocol\n"
"    Ports []Port\n"
"    "
