#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:3
msgid ""
"These markers describe how [webhook configuration](../webhook-overview.md) "
"is generated. Use these to keep the description of your webhooks close to "
"the code that implements them."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:9 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:32
msgid ""
"It specifies only the details that are intrinsic to the application serving "
"it (e.g. the resources it can handle, or the path it serves on)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:12 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:35
msgid "Example (Validating Webhook):"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:14 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:37
msgid ""
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:webhook:path=/validate-mygroup-v1-myresource,mutating=false,failurePolicy=fail,sideEffects=None,groups=mygroup.example.com,resources=myresources,verbs=create;update,versions=v1,name=myresource.kb.io,admissionReviewVersions=v1\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:16 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:39
msgid "Example (Mutating Webhook):"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:18 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:41
msgid ""
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:webhook:path=/mutate-mygroup-v1-myresource,mutating=true,failurePolicy=fail,sideEffects=None,groups=mygroup.example.com,resources=myresources,verbs=create;update,versions=v1,name=myresource.kb.io,admissionReviewVersions=v1\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:22 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:68
msgid ""
"Mutating webhooks are allowed to change the object in their response, and "
"are called _before_ all validating webhooks.  Mutating webhooks may choose "
"to reject an object, similarly to a validating webhook."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:28 src/reference/markers/webhook.md:74
msgid "Example: \"myresource.mygroup.example.com\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:45
msgid ""
"versions the Webhook expects. The API server will try to use the first "
"version in the list which it supports. If none of the versions specified are "
"supported, the API call will fail. Common values: \"v1\" or \"v1;v1beta1\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:51
msgid ""
"It may be either \"ignore\" (to skip the webhook and continue on) or "
"\"fail\" (to reject the object in question). Most webhooks should use "
"\"fail\" to ensure the webhook logic is always executed."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:57
msgid ""
"Use \"_\" to match all groups. Multiple groups are separated by semicolons. "
"Example: \"apps;batch\" or \"_\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:62
msgid ""
"Allowed values are \"Exact\" (match only if it exactly matches the specified "
"rule) or \"Equivalent\" (match a request if it modifies a resource listed in "
"rules, even via another API group or version). Defaults to \"Equivalent\" if "
"not specified."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:78
msgid ""
"This allows you to set any webhook field that isn't directly exposed as a "
"marker parameter, such as namespaceSelector, objectSelector, or "
"matchConditions. The patch is a JSON object that follows Kubernetes "
"strategic merge patch semantics and is applied to the webhook configuration "
"after all other marker parameters are processed."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:83
msgid "Use backticks to avoid escaping quotes in the JSON."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:85
msgid "Common use cases:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:86
msgid "Limit webhook scope to specific namespaces using namespaceSelector"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:87
msgid "Filter webhook invocations by object labels using objectSelector"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:88
msgid "Combine multiple customizations in a single patch"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:90
msgid "Example (limit to labeled namespaces):"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:92
msgid ""
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:webhook:path=/mutate-v1-pod,mutating=true,...,patch=`{\"namespaceSelector\":{\"matchLabels\":{\"webhook-enabled\":\"true\"}}}`\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:94
msgid "Example (filter by object labels with matchExpressions):"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:96
msgid ""
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:webhook:path=/validate-v1-deployment,...,patch=`{\"objectSelector\":{\"matchExpressions\":[{\"key\":\"tier\",\"operator\":\"In\",\"values\":[\"frontend\",\"backend\"]}]}}`\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:98
msgid "Example (combine namespace and object selectors):"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:100
msgid ""
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:webhook:...,patch=`{\"namespaceSelector\":{\"matchLabels\":{\"env\":\"production\"}},\"objectSelector\":{\"matchLabels\":{\"managed-by\":\"my-operator\"}}}`\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:102
msgid "Example (override timeout):"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:104
msgid "    // +kubebuilder:webhook:...,patch=`{\"timeoutSeconds\":25}`\n    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:106
msgid "Example (remove a field by setting it to null):"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:108
msgid "    // +kubebuilder:webhook:...,patch=`{\"timeoutSeconds\":null}`\n    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:110
msgid ""
"Setting a field to null removes it. Patching a list field without a merge "
"key, such as rules, replaces the whole list. Field names are case-sensitive "
"and unknown fields in the patch cause an error."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:116
msgid ""
"prefixed with a '/validate-' or '/mutate-' depending on the type, and "
"followed by $GROUP-$VERSION-$KIND where all values are lower-cased and the "
"periods in the group are substituted for hyphens. For example, a validating "
"webhook path for type batch.tutorial.kubebuilder.io/v1,Kind=CronJob would be "
"/validate-batch-tutorial-kubebuilder-io-v1-cronjob"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:124
msgid ""
"To allow mutating admission plugins to observe changes made by other "
"plugins, built-in mutating admission plugins are re-run if a mutating "
"webhook modifies an object, and mutating webhooks can specify a "
"reinvocationPolicy to control whether they are reinvoked as well. May be "
"\"Never\" or \"IfNeeded\". Defaults to \"Never\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:131
msgid ""
"Use \"_\" to match all resources. Multiple resources are separated by "
"semicolons. Example: \"deployments;pods\" or \"_\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:136
msgid "Defaults to \"webhook-service\" if not specified."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:140
msgid "Defaults to \"system\" if not specified."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:144
msgid "Defaults to 443 if not specified."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:148
msgid ""
"This has an impact on dry runs and `kubectl diff`: if the sideEffect is "
"\"Unknown\" (the default) or \"Some\", then the API server will not call the "
"webhook on a dry-run request and fails instead. If the value is \"None\", "
"then the webhook has no side effects and the API server will call it on "
"dry-run. If the value is \"NoneOnDryRun\", then the webhook is responsible "
"for inspecting the \"dryRun\" property of the AdmissionReview sent in the "
"request, and avoiding side effects if that value is \"true.\" Most webhooks "
"should use \"None\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:157
msgid ""
"If the timeout expires before the webhook responds, the webhook call will be "
"ignored or the API call will be rejected based on the failure policy. The "
"timeout value must be between 1 and 30 seconds. The timeout for an admission "
"webhook defaults to 10 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:163
msgid ""
"the manifests, instead of using the internal service communication. Should "
"be in format of https://address:port/path When this option is specified, the "
"serviceConfig.Service is removed from webhook the manifest. The URL "
"configuration should be between quotes. `url` cannot be specified when "
"`path` is specified."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:171
msgid ""
"Only modification-like verbs may be specified. May be \"create\", "
"\"update\", \"delete\", \"connect\", or \"\\*\" (for all). Multiple verbs "
"are separated by semicolons. Example: \"create;update\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:177
msgid ""
"Use \"_\" to match all versions. Multiple versions are separated by "
"semicolons. Example: \"v1;v1beta1\" or \"_\"."
