"`--ssa` flag enables this generation and for examples of using the generated "
"types."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:3
msgid ""
"These markers cause an [RBAC "
"ClusterRole](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/rbac/#role-and-clusterrole) "
"to be generated.  This allows you to describe the permissions that your "
"controller requires alongside the code that makes use of those permissions."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:11
msgid ""
"RBAC markers are used to generate ClusterRole or Role manifests. Multiple "
"markers can be combined to build comprehensive RBAC policies."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:16
msgid ""
"    // Basic resource access\n"
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,resources=deployments,verbs=get;list;watch\n"
"    \n"
"    // Core API group (use empty string)\n"
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:rbac:groups=&#34;&#34;,resources=pods;services,verbs=get;list;watch\n"
"    \n"
"    // Multiple API groups and resources\n"
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps;batch,resources=deployments;jobs,verbs=get;list;watch;create;update;patch;delete\n"
"    \n"
"    // Access to resource status or scale subresources\n"
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,resources=deployments/status,verbs=get;update;patch\n"
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,resources=deployments/scale,verbs=get;update\n"
"    \n"
"    // Access to specific resource instances by name\n"
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:rbac:groups=&#34;&#34;,resources=configmaps,resourceNames=my-config,verbs=get\n"
"    \n"
"    // Non-resource URLs (for metrics, healthz, etc.)\n"
"    // +kubebuilder:rbac:urls=/metrics;/healthz,verbs=get\n"
"    \n"
"    // Namespace-scoped Role instead of ClusterRole\n"
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:rbac:groups=&#34;&#34;,namespace=my-namespace,resources=secrets,verbs=get;list;watch\n"
"    \n"
"    // Custom role name\n"
"    // "
"+kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,resources=deployments,verbs=get;list,roleName=deployment-reader\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:43
msgid ""
"Use empty string (\"\") for the core API group. Multiple groups can be "
"specified separated by semicolons. Example: \"apps;batch\" or \"\" (for core "
"group)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:49
msgid ""
"If not set, the Rule belongs to the generated ClusterRole. If set, the Rule "
"belongs to a Role, whose namespace is specified by this field. Example: "
"\"my-namespace\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:55
msgid ""
"Create requests cannot be restricted by resourcename, as the object's name "
"is not known at authorization time. Multiple names can be specified "
"separated by semicolons. Example: \"my-config;my-secret\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:62
msgid ""
"Multiple resources can be specified separated by semicolons. Subresources "
"can be specified with a slash (e.g., \"deployments/status\"). Example: "
"\"deployments;pods\" or \"deployments/status\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:68
msgid ""
"If not set, uses the default roleName from the generator. Useful for "
"avoiding name conflicts when the same roleName is used across multiple "
"namespaces."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:71
msgid ""
"Example: When using namespace-scoped RBAC markers with kustomize's global "
"namespace transformation, multiple Roles might end up in the same namespace "
"with identical names, causing an \"ID conflict\" error. Use roleName to "
"ensure each Role has a unique name:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:75
msgid ""
"// "
"+kubebuilder:rbac:groups=apps,namespace=infrastructure,roleName=infra-manager,resources=deployments,verbs=get;list "
"// "
"+kubebuilder:rbac:groups=\"\",namespace=users,roleName=user-secrets,resources=secrets,verbs=get"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:78
msgid ""
"This generates Roles named \"infra-manager\" and \"user-secrets\" instead of "
"both being \"manager-role\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:82
msgid ""
"Non-resource URLs are paths that don't represent resources, like "
"\"/metrics\" or \"/healthz\". Multiple URLs can be specified separated by "
"semicolons. Example: \"/metrics;/healthz\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:88
msgid ""
"Common verbs: \"get\", \"list\", \"watch\", \"create\", \"update\", "
"\"patch\", \"delete\". Use \"\\*\" for all verbs. Multiple verbs must be "
"specified separated by semicolons. Example: \"get;list;watch\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:3
msgid ""
"The `+kubebuilder:scaffold` marker is a key part of the Kubebuilder "
"scaffolding system. It marks locations in generated files where Kubebuilder "
"injects additional code as you scaffold new resources (such as controllers, "
"webhooks, or APIs). This enables Kubebuilder to seamlessly integrate newly "
"generated components into the project without affecting user-defined code."
