#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:1
msgid "Sub-module layouts"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:3
msgid ""
"This part describes how to modify a scaffolded project for use with multiple "
"`go.mod` files for APIs and Controllers."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:5
msgid ""
"Sub-Module Layouts (in a way you could call them a special form of "
"[Monorepo's](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monorepo)) are a special use case "
"and can help in scenarios that involve reuse of APIs without introducing "
"indirect dependencies that should not be available in the project consuming "
"the API externally."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:10
msgid ""
"If you are looking to do operations and reconcile via a controller a "
"Type(CRD) which are owned by another project or By Kubernetes API then, "
"please see [Using an external "
"Resources/API](/reference/using_an_external_resource.md) for more info."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:18
msgid ""
"Separate `go.mod` modules for APIs and Controllers can help for the "
"following cases:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:20
msgid ""
"There is an enterprise version of an operator available that wants to reuse "
"APIs from the Community Version"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:21
msgid ""
"There are many (possibly external) modules depending on the API and you want "
"to have a more strict separation of transitive dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:22
msgid ""
"If you want to reduce impact of transitive dependencies on your API being "
"included in other projects"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:23
msgid ""
"If you are looking to separately manage the lifecycle of your API release "
"process from your controller release process."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:24
msgid ""
"If you are looking to modularize your codebase without splitting your code "
"between multiple repositories."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:26
msgid ""
"They introduce however multiple caveats into typical projects which is one "
"of the main factors that makes them hard to recommend in a generic use-case "
"or plugin:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:28
msgid ""
"Multiple `go.mod` modules are not recommended as a go best practice and "
"[multiple modules are mostly "
"discouraged](https://github.com/golang/go/wiki/Modules#faqs--multi-module-repositories)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:29
msgid ""
"There is always the possibility to extract your APIs into a new repository "
"and arguably also have more control over the release process in a project "
"spanning multiple repos relying on the same API types."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:30
msgid ""
"It requires at least one [replace "
"directive](https://go.dev/ref/mod#go-mod-file-replace) either through "
"`go.work` which is at least 2 more files plus an environment variable for "
"build environments without GO_WORK or through `go.mod` replace, which has to "
"be manually dropped and added for every release."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:35
msgid ""
"When deciding to deviate from the standard kubebuilder `PROJECT` setup or "
"the extended layouts offered by its plugins, it can result in increased "
"maintenance overhead as there can be breaking changes in upstream that could "
"break with the custom module structure described here."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:37
msgid ""
"Splitting your codebase to multiple repos and/or multiple modules incurs "
"costs that grow over time. You need to define clear version dependencies "
"between your own modules, do phased upgrades carefully, etc. Especially for "
"small-to-medium projects, one repo and one module is the best way to go."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:39
msgid ""
"Bear in mind, that it is not recommended to deviate from the proposed layout "
"unless you know what you are doing. You may also lose the ability to use "
"some of the CLI features and helpers. For further information on the project "
"layout, see the doc [What's in a basic "
"project?](./../cronjob-tutorial/basic-project.md)"
msgstr ""

