#: src/reference/using_an_external_resource.md:1
msgid "Using external resources"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/using_an_external_resource.md:3
msgid ""
"In some cases, your project may need to work with resources that are not "
"defined by your own APIs. These external resources fall into two main "
"categories:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/using_an_external_resource.md:6
msgid ""
"**Core Types**: API types defined by Kubernetes itself, such as `Pods`, "
"`Services`, and `Deployments`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/using_an_external_resource.md:7
msgid ""
"**External Types**: API types defined in other projects, such as CRDs "
"defined by another solution."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/using_an_external_resource.md:9
msgid "Managing external types"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/using_an_external_resource.md:11
msgid "Creating a controller for external types"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/using_an_external_resource.md:13
msgid ""
"To create a controller for an external type without scaffolding a resource, "
"use the `create api` command with the `--resource=false` option and specify "
"the path to the external API type using the `--external-api-path` and "
"`--external-api-domain` flag options. This generates a controller for types "
"defined outside your project, such as CRDs managed by other Operators."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/using_an_external_resource.md:19
msgid "The command looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/using_an_external_resource.md:25
msgid ""
"`--external-api-path`: Provide the Go import path where you define the "
"external types."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/using_an_external_resource.md:26
msgid ""
"`--external-api-domain`: Provide the domain for the external types. "
"Kubebuilder uses this value to generate RBAC permissions and create the "
"QualifiedGroup, such as - `apiGroups: <group>.<domain>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/using_an_external_resource.md:28
msgid "For example, if you are managing Certificates from Cert Manager:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/using_an_external_resource.md:37
msgid ""
"You can pin a specific version of the external API dependency using the "
"`--external-api-module` flag:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/using_an_external_resource.md:47
msgid ""
"The flag accepts the module path with optional version (e.g., "
"`github.com/cert-manager/cert-manager@v1.18.2`). The module is stored in the "
"PROJECT file and added to `go.mod` using `go get`, which cleanly adds it as "
"a direct dependency without polluting go.mod with unnecessary indirect "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

