#: src/reference/envtest.md:185
msgid "Testing considerations"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/envtest.md:187
msgid ""
"Unless you are using an existing cluster, keep in mind that no built-in "
"controllers run in the test context. In some ways, the test control plane "
"behaves differently from \"real\" clusters, and that might impact how you "
"write tests. One common example is garbage collection; because no "
"controllers monitor built-in resources, Kubernetes does not delete objects, "
"even if you set up an `OwnerReference`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/envtest.md:189
msgid ""
"To test that the deletion lifecycle works, test the ownership instead of "
"asserting on existence. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/envtest.md:193
msgid "\"MyCoolCustomResource\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/envtest.md:194
msgid "\"my.api.example.com/v1beta1\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/envtest.md:195
msgid "\"d9607e19-f88f-11e6-a518-42010a800195\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/envtest.md:196
msgid "\"userSpecifiedResourceName\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/envtest.md:205
msgid ""
"EnvTest does not support namespace deletion. Deleting a namespace seems to "
"succeed, but Kubernetes just puts the namespace in a Terminating state, and "
"never actually reclaims it. Trying to recreate the namespace fails. This "
"causes your reconciler to continue reconciling any objects left behind, "
"unless you delete them."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/envtest.md:207
msgid ""
"To overcome this limitation you can create a new namespace for each test. "
"Even so, when one test completes (e.g. in \"namespace-1\") and another test "
"starts (e.g. in \"namespace-2\"), the controller will still be reconciling "
"any active objects from \"namespace-1\". This can be avoided by ensuring "
"that all tests clean up after themselves as part of the test teardown.  If "
"teardown of a namespace is difficult, it may be possible to wire the "
"reconciler in such a way that it ignores reconcile requests that come from "
"namespaces other than the one being tested:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/envtest.md:213
msgid "// restrict namespaces to reconcile\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/envtest.md:216
msgid "\"myreconciler\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/envtest.md:217
