#: src/reference/project-config.md:72
msgid "Why store the plugins and data used?"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:74
msgid "Following some examples of motivations to track the input used:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:75
msgid ""
"check if a plugin can or cannot be scaffolded on top of an existing plugin "
"(i.e.) plugin compatibility while chaining multiple of them together."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:76
msgid ""
"what operations can or cannot be done such as verify if the layout allows "
"API(s) for different groups to be scaffolded for the current configuration "
"or not."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:77
msgid ""
"verify what data can or cannot be used in the CLI operations such as to "
"ensure that WebHooks can only be created for pre-existent API(s)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:79
msgid ""
"Note that KubeBuilder is not only a CLI tool but can also be used as a "
"library to allow users to create their plugins/tools, provide helpers and "
"customizations on top of their existing projects - an example of which is "
"[Operator-SDK](https://sdk.operatorframework.io/). SDK leverages KubeBuilder "
"to create plugins to allow users to work with other languages and provide "
"helpers for their users to integrate their projects with, for example, the "
"[Operator Framework solutions/OLM](https://olm.operatorframework.io/). You "
"can check the [plugin's "
"documentation](../plugins/creating-plugins.html#why-use-the-kubebuilder-style) "
"to know more about creating custom plugins."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:81
msgid ""
"Additionally, another motivation for the PROJECT file is to help us to "
"create a feature that allows users to easily upgrade their projects by "
"providing helpers that automatically re-scaffold the project. By having all "
"the required metadata regarding the APIs, their configurations and versions "
"in the PROJECT file. For example, it can be used to automate the process of "
"re-scaffolding while migrating between plugin versions. ([More "
"info](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/blob/master/designs/helper_to_upgrade_projects_by_rescaffolding.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:83
msgid "Versioning"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:85
msgid ""
"The Project config is versioned according to its layout. For further "
"information see "
"[Versioning](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/blob/master/VERSIONING.md#Versioning)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:87
msgid "Layout definition"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:89
msgid "The `PROJECT` version `3` layout looks like:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:105
#: src/plugins/extending/extending_cli_features_and_plugins.md:429
msgid "memcached:memcached:1.6.26-alpine3.19"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:112
#: src/plugins/extending/extending_cli_features_and_plugins.md:436
msgid "busybox:1.36.1"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:149
msgid "Now let us check its layout fields definition:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:151
msgid "Field"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:153
msgid "`cliVersion`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:153
msgid ""
"Used to record the specific CLI version used during project scaffolding with "
"`init`. Helps identifying the version of the tooling employed, aiding in "
"troubleshooting and ensuring compatibility with updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:154
msgid "`layout`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:154
msgid ""
"Defines the global plugins, e.g. a project `init` with "
"`--plugins=\"go/v4,deploy-image/v1-alpha\"` means that any sub-command used "
"will always call its implementation for both plugins in a chain."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:155
msgid "`domain`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:155
msgid ""
"Store the domain of the project. This information can be provided by the "
"user when the project is generate with the `init` sub-command and the "
"`domain` flag."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:156
msgid "`plugins`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:156
msgid ""
"Defines the plugins used to do custom scaffolding, e.g. to use the optional "
"`deploy-image/v1-alpha` plugin to do scaffolding for just a specific api via "
"the command `kubebuider create api [options] "
"--plugins=deploy-image/v1-alpha`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:157
msgid "`projectName`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:157
msgid ""
"The name of the project. This is used to scaffold the manager data. By "
"default it is the name of the project directory, however, it can be provided "
"by the user in the `init` sub-command via the `--project-name` flag."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:158
msgid "`repo`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:158
msgid ""
"The project repository which is the Golang module, e.g "
"`github.com/example/myproject-operator`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:159
msgid "`multigroup`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:159
msgid ""
"**(Optional)** When set to `true`, enables multi-group project layout. APIs "
"are organized into group-specific directories (`api/<group>/<version>/`). "
"Can be set during initialization via `kubebuilder init --multigroup` or "
"enabled/disabled later via `kubebuilder edit --multigroup`. Default is "
"`false` (omitted from PROJECT file)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:160
msgid "`namespaced`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:160
msgid ""
"**(Optional)** When set to `true`, configures the project for "
"namespace-scoped deployment. The operator will only watch and manage "
"resources within its deployment namespace, using namespace-scoped RBAC "
"(`Role`/`RoleBinding` instead of `ClusterRole`/`ClusterRoleBinding`). Can be "
"enabled/disabled via `kubebuilder edit --namespaced`. Default is `false` "
"(cluster-scoped, omitted from PROJECT file)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:161
msgid "`resources`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:161
msgid "An array of all resources that you scaffolded in the project."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:162
msgid "`resources.api`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:162
msgid "The API scaffolded in the project via the sub-command `create api`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:163
msgid "`resources.api.crdVersion`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:163
msgid ""
"The Kubernetes API version (`apiVersion`) used to do the scaffolding for the "
"CRD resource."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:164
msgid "`resources.api.namespaced`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:164
msgid "The API RBAC permissions which can be namespaced or cluster scoped."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:165
msgid "`resources.api.ssa`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:165
msgid ""
"**(Optional, Alpha)** When set to `true`, the API was scaffolded with "
"Server-Side Apply support via `create api --ssa`. The scaffold adds the "
"`+genclient` marker and generates apply configurations for the type. Alpha "
"feature: it may change in future releases. Default is `false` (omitted from "
"the PROJECT file)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:166
msgid "`resources.controller`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:166
msgid "Indicates whether you scaffolded a controller for the API."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:167
msgid "`resources.domain`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:167
msgid ""
"The domain of the resource that you provided by the `--domain` flag when you "
"initialized the project or via the flag `--external-api-domain` when you "
"used it to scaffold controllers for an [External "
"Type](./using_an_external_resource.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:168
msgid "`resources.group`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:168
msgid ""
"The GKV group of the resource that you provide by the `--group` flag when "
"you use the sub-command `create api`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:169
msgid "`resources.version`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:169
msgid ""
"The GKV version of the resource that you provide by the `--version` flag "
"when you use the sub-command `create api`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:170
msgid "`resources.kind`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:170
msgid ""
"Stores the GKV Kind of the resource that you provide by the `--kind` flag "
"when you use the sub-command `create api`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-config.md:171
