#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:1
msgid "Versions compatibility and supportability"
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:3
msgid ""
"Projects created by Kubebuilder contain a `Makefile` that installs tools at "
"versions defined during project creation. The main tools included are:"
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:6
msgid "[kustomize](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kustomize)"
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:7
msgid "[controller-gen](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-tools)"
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:8
msgid ""
"[setup-envtest](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-runtime/tree/main/tools/setup-envtest)"
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:10
msgid ""
"Additionally, these projects include a `go.mod` file specifying dependency "
"versions. Kubebuilder relies on "
"[controller-runtime](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-runtime) "
"and its Go and Kubernetes dependencies. Therefore, the versions defined in "
"the `Makefile` and `go.mod` files are the ones that have been tested, "
"supported, and recommended."
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:14
msgid ""
"Each minor version of Kubebuilder is tested with a specific minor version of "
"client-go. While a Kubebuilder minor version _may_ be compatible with other "
"client-go minor versions, or other tools, this compatibility is not "
"guaranteed, supported, or tested."
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:18
msgid ""
"The minimum Go version required by Kubebuilder is determined by the highest "
"minimum Go version required by its dependencies. This is usually aligned "
"with the minimum Go version required by the corresponding `k8s.io/*` "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:22
msgid ""
"Compatible `k8s.io/*` versions, client-go versions, and minimum Go versions "
"can be found in the `go.mod` file scaffolded for each project for each [tag "
"release](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/tags)."
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:25
msgid ""
"**Example:** For the `4.1.1` release, the minimum Go version compatibility "
"is `1.22`. You can refer to the samples in the testdata directory of the tag "
"released "
"[v4.1.1](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/tree/v4.1.1/testdata), "
"such as the "
"[go.mod](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/blob/v4.1.1/testdata/project-v4/go.mod#L3) "
"file for `project-v4`. You can also check the tools versions supported and "
"tested for this release by examining the "
"[Makefile](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/blob/v4.1.1/testdata/project-v4/Makefile#L160-L165)."
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:30
msgid "Operating systems supported"
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:32
msgid ""
"Kubebuilder officially supports macOS and Linux platforms. If you are using "
"Windows, see the [Windows "
"instructions](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/blob/master/docs/windows.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:34
msgid "Contributions towards supporting Windows are not planned."
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:39
msgid ""
"After using the CLI to create your project, you are free to customize it as "
"you see fit. Bear in mind, that it is not recommended to deviate from the "
"proposed layout unless you know what you are doing."
msgstr ""

#: src/versions_compatibility_supportability.md:43
msgid ""
"For example, you should refrain from moving the scaffolded files; doing so "
"makes it difficult to upgrade your project in the future. You may also lose "
"the ability to use some of the CLI features and helpers. For further "
"information on the project layout, see the doc [What's in a basic "
"project?](./cronjob-tutorial/basic-project.md)"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/plugins.md:3
msgid ""
"Kubebuilder's architecture is fundamentally plugin-based. This design "
"enables the Kubebuilder CLI to evolve while maintaining backward "
"compatibility with older versions, allowing users to opt-in or opt-out of "
"specific features, and enabling seamless integration with external tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/plugins.md:9
msgid ""
"By leveraging plugins, projects can extend Kubebuilder and use it as a "
"library to support new functionalities or implement custom scaffolding "
"tailored to their users' needs. This flexibility allows maintainers to build "
"on top of Kubebuilder’s foundation, adapting it to specific use cases while "
"benefiting from its powerful scaffolding engine."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/plugins.md:15
msgid "Plugins offer several key advantages:"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/plugins.md:17
msgid ""
"**Backward compatibility**: Ensures older layouts and project structures "
"remain functional with newer versions."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/plugins.md:18
msgid ""
"**Customization**: Allows users to opt-in or opt-out for specific features "
"(i.e. [Grafana](./available/grafana-v1-alpha.md) and [Deploy "
"Image](./available/deploy-image-plugin-v1-alpha.md) plugins)"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/plugins.md:19
msgid ""
"**Extensibility**: Facilitates integration with third-party tools and "
"projects that wish to provide their own [External "
"Plugins](./extending/external-plugins.md), which can be used alongside "
"Kubebuilder to modify and enhance project scaffolding or introduce new "
"features."
msgstr ""

