"`templates/manager/manager.yaml`, you needs to manually reapply your "
"customizations on top of the latest changes after regenerating the Helm "
"chart."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/available/helm-v1-alpha.md:56
#: src/plugins/available/helm-v2-alpha.md:136
msgid ""
"Although [Helm best "
"practices](https://helm.sh/docs/chart_best_practices/custom_resource_definitions/#method-1-let-helm-do-it-for-you) "
"recommend placing CRDs under a top-level `crds/` directory, the Kubebuilder "
"Helm plugin intentionally places them under `templates/crd`."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/available/helm-v1-alpha.md:58
msgid ""
"The rationale is tied to how Helm itself handles CRDs. By default, Helm "
"installs CRDs once during the initial release, but it will **ignore CRD "
"changes** on subsequent upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/available/helm-v1-alpha.md:62
#: src/plugins/available/helm-v2-alpha.md:140
msgid ""
"This can lead to surprising behavior where chart upgrades silently skip CRD "
"updates, leaving clusters out of sync."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/available/helm-v1-alpha.md:65
#: src/plugins/available/helm-v2-alpha.md:142
msgid ""
"To avoid endorsing this behavior, the Kubebuilder plugin follows the "
"approach of packaging CRDs inside `templates/`. In this mode, Helm treats "
"CRDs like any other resource, ensuring they are applied and upgraded as "
"expected. While this prevents mixing CRDs and CRs of the same type in a "
"single chart (since Helm cannot wait between creation steps), it ensures "
"predictable and explicit lifecycle management of CRDs."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/available/helm-v1-alpha.md:70
#: src/plugins/available/helm-v2-alpha.md:144
msgid "In short:"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/available/helm-v1-alpha.md:71
msgid "**Helm `crds/` directory** → one-time install only, no upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/available/helm-v1-alpha.md:72
msgid ""
"**Kubebuilder `templates/crd`** → CRDs managed like other manifests, "
"upgrades included."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/available/helm-v1-alpha.md:74
#: src/plugins/available/helm-v2-alpha.md:148
msgid ""
"This design choice prioritizes correctness and maintainability over Helm's "
"default convention, while leaving room for future improvements (such as "
"scaffolding separate charts for APIs and controllers)."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/available/helm-v1-alpha.md:82
msgid ""
"The Helm plugin is attached to the `edit` subcommand as the `helm/v1-alpha` "
"plugin relies on the Go project being scaffolded first."
