#: src/faq.md:179
msgid ""
"When I build the image with Podman or Buildah, the build fails with "
"`cmd/main.go: no such file or directory`. How to solve it?"
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:181 src/faq.md:197
msgid ""
"While we do our best to keep the scaffold working with other container "
"tools, Kubebuilder is officially tested and supported with **Docker**."
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:183
msgid ""
"The scaffolded `.dockerignore` re-includes all Go source files with "
"`!**/*.go`. Docker honors this pattern. Podman and Buildah do not: they skip "
"ignored directories, so no Go source reaches the build context. This is "
"tracked upstream in "
"[buildah#6417](https://github.com/containers/buildah/issues/6417) and was "
"reported in "
"[kubebuilder#5181](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/issues/5181)."
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:185
msgid ""
"If you use Podman, re-include your source directories by name in "
"`.dockerignore`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:193
msgid "Add any other directory in your project that holds Go source files."
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:195
msgid ""
"When I build the image with Podman or Buildah I get `short-name "
"\"golang:1.26\" did not resolve to an alias and no unqualified-search "
"registries are defined`. How to solve it?"
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:199
msgid ""
"Docker resolves short image names to Docker Hub. Podman and Buildah resolve "
"them from the host, using either the [short-name "
"aliases](https://github.com/containers/shortnames) in "
"[`registries.conf.d`](https://github.com/containers/image/blob/main/docs/containers-registries.conf.d.5.md) "
"or `unqualified-search-registries` in "
"[`registries.conf`](https://github.com/containers/image/blob/main/docs/containers-registries.conf.5.md). "
"You hit this error when the host has neither. Debian 12, for example, ships "
"neither."
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:201
msgid "Use one of the options below."
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:203
msgid ""
"**Override the base image.** The scaffolded `Dockerfile` exposes it as a "
"[build "
"argument](https://docs.docker.com/reference/dockerfile/#understand-how-arg-and-from-interact):"
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:211
msgid "# From Docker Hub\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:213
msgid "# From your own registry or mirror\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:218
msgid "`make docker-buildx` accepts `BASE_IMAGE` too."
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:220
msgid "**Or add an alias on the host** for the `golang` short name:"
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:222
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# /etc/containers/registries.conf.d/golang.conf\n"
"[aliases]\n"
"\"golang\" = \"docker.io/library/golang\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/faq.md:228
msgid ""
"A matching alias is used without consulting `unqualified-search-registries`, "
"so it works even when that list is empty. It also ignores the tag, so one "
"entry covers all `golang` tags. Prefer it over adding `docker.io` to the "
"search list, which changes how every unqualified image name resolves on the "
"host. For rootless Podman, use "
"`$HOME/.config/containers/registries.conf.d/golang.conf`."
msgstr ""

